For any $t\in [0,T],$ there exists a linear space $V\subset H$ of dimension $C_{\mathcal L}|\log(\epsilon)|^2$ such that \begin{align}\label{add-over-err}
   \|u(t)-P_{V}u(t)\|_{L^2(\Omega;H)}\lesssim  \epsilon (1+\|u_0\|_{L^2(\Omega;H)})\;. 
   \end{align}

Then there exists a subspace $V$ of dimension $o(\epsilon^{-\frac 2{p}})$ such that 
 \begin{align}\label{err-formula-hyper}
    \|P_V u-u\|_{L^2(\Omega;L^2([0,T];H))}\lesssim \epsilon.
 \end{align}

